ctlsock: when the only cursor register is guest RAM, READ it — a window into a save item

Applies AFTER mame-ctlsock-abs-ram.patch (same file, later hunks). Env-only:
unset, every existing station builds and behaves byte for byte as before.

THE WALL (apple2gs, MEASURED 2026-09-13 — docs/lab/APPLE2GS-WAVE.md §7-§9).
The Apple IIGS keeps its cursor position in guest RAM, at $E1/00E9 (X) and
$E1/00EB (Y), 16-bit little-endian, in GUEST pixels. That is a perfect live
sensor — and the macsys1 WRITE route does not work on it: poking those words
sticks but never redraws, and the next ADB poll republishes them from an
accumulator that is in neither banks $00/$01/$E0/$E1 nor the ADB micro's own
256 bytes. The five RAM copies are OUTPUTS. So the GS cannot be driven
absolutely; it can only be driven closed-loop, and for that MOVEA needs to
READ $E1/00E9 every window.

It nearly could already. `m_megaii_ram` is a registered save item — size=1,
count=131072, covering banks $E0/$E1 — so $E1/00E9 is byte offset 0x100E9
inside an item the module can already resolve. What was missing was the
ability to address INSIDE an item, and to convert a GUEST-pixel reading into
a PUBLISHED one.

THE FIX, two small pieces:

  1. A cursor item may now be `suffix@offset[:width]` — a little-endian
     integer of `width` bytes (default 2) at byte `offset` in a byte-sized
     save item. `save_item_handle` carries the window (win_off/win_w) and
     read() assembles it; width 0 is the historical path, untouched. A window
     that cannot be read (wrong element size, past the end) DROPS the handle
     with a log line rather than becoming a silent zero sensor, so MOVEA
     degrades to open loop the same way an unresolved suffix does.

  2. MAME_CTL_CAL_SX / MAME_CTL_CAL_SY, a multiplicative scale beside the
     existing CAL_X/CAL_Y offset: published = CAL + reading * CAL_S. A
     cursor register that already reads in published pixels (irix's VC2)
     defaults to 1.0 and is unchanged; the GS's guest-pixel reading becomes
     published via 47 + gx*1.4531 and 53 + gy*3.325 — the measured inset and
     aspect scale of the 640x200 SHR raster inside the 1024x768 surface.

Nothing else changes: the MOVEA V7 engine, its gain learning, the pacing
window and the give-up cap all run exactly as they do on irix, now against a
reading instead of a belief.

MEASURED on apple2gs (rig1 restored from the golden, five targets x two laps
on the published surface, cursor readback via $E1/00E9): see
docs/lab/APPLE2GS-WAVE.md §11. The loop can only land on guest-pixel centres
— one ADB count is one guest pixel — so its resolution bound is +/-0.73 px on
X and +/-1.66 px on Y in published pixels.

